    Idempotency-Key for the routes that move money (utils/idempotency.ts)
    
    The first request with a key claims IDEM#<caller>#<key> in v2CustomerTable and
    stores its answer; a retry of the same request gets that answer again, marked
    Idempotent-Replayed, and runs nothing. Another request on the key, or one still
    running, answers 409 100061; a handler that throws leaves its key claimed until
    it expires (24 h), never run twice on its own. Routes opt in; withdraw, transfer
    and deposit take it as optional, so requests without one run as before.
    v2CustomerTable gets a ttl attribute and both APIs allow the header (step 1.4).

